  "facts": [
    "Lansdowne Bridge, a sandstone marvel, spans Prospect Creek with a 110‑foot (34 m) single arch, the largest surviving masonry span in Australia, completed by convicts between 1834 and 1836.",
    "Designed by Scottish mason David Lennox, the bridge was inaugurated on 26 January 1836, the colony’s 48th anniversary, after Governor Bourke laid the foundation stone on 1 January 1834.",
    "In 1956, a concrete arch duplicate was built to carry southbound traffic, preserving the original’s heritage while accommodating modern Hume Highway demands."
